paragraph('Once the model is calibrated, it can also', r'''A configured HWQM can be used offline to examine the transport consequences of a hypothetical contaminant release. The example here concerns construction-related nitrogen inputs and illustrates how the integrated framework supports scenario analysis. Figures~\ref{fig:contam} and \ref{fig:contamtime1} retain outputs from an earlier scenario configuration, not the revised thermal run in Table~\ref{tab:performance}. No release was observed, and the sparse laboratory nitrogen samples cannot resolve a transient plume. These outputs therefore demonstrate the analysis workflow rather than validated concentration forecasts.''')
