span(r'\subsection{Latency}', r'\section[\appendixname~\thesection]{Stability', r'''\subsection{Computational throughput and latency}

Nine supplied full-season runs with a common mesh and vertical discretization completed 212 simulated days in a median 32.5~minutes under twelve MPI partitions on the machine in Table~\ref{tab:computer}. This corresponds to approximately 9,400 simulated seconds per wall-clock second. It is a solver-throughput benchmark, not a measured duration for an hourly restart or an end-to-end operational update. It is also distinct from the serial historical campaign behind Figure~\ref{fig:meshconverge}.

Hourly acquisition makes near-real-time updates a plausible target, but total latency also includes retrieval, preparation, model execution, selection and publication. The full interval has not been measured. Twice-daily profiles additionally have a coarser observation cadence. The framework therefore does not claim a demonstrated under-two-hour publication latency.

\subsection{Robustness}

Gap handling and data-quality processing are implemented components. End-to-end behaviour under retrieval failures, incomplete forcing and failed simulations has not been established through operational testing. Retention of the last successful output, explicit timestamps and stale-data alerts are requirements for a future unattended service, rather than demonstrated properties of this prototype.''')
